  "aiContextParagraph": "Following the latest national elections, Israeli President Isaac Herzog has designated opposition figure Gadi Eisenkot as the individual responsible for building a new government. This mandate grants Eisenkot a six-week period to secure a governing majority within the legislature. The political situation remains fluid as Eisenkot works to navigate the complexities of coalition-building, including efforts to reach out to factions historically aligned with the incumbent, Benjamin Netanyahu. Analysts and international observers are closely monitoring these developments to determine if the newcomer can successfully displace the current Prime Minister or if the process will lead to alternative political scenarios. The current phase follows a period of electoral activity, and the outcome of these negotiations will define the composition of the next administration. Failure to form a government within the allotted timeframe may prompt further constitutional procedures or alternative political arrangements to resolve the current deadlock.",
